WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.500
Right now.

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:01.001
Can you give

00:00:01.001 --> 00:00:04.270
us any up to date information

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:06.873
about what's happening around that dam?

00:00:06.873 --> 00:00:09.676
It's obviously a catastrophic breach

00:00:09.976 --> 00:00:12.712
and it's affected huge numbers of people

00:00:12.912 --> 00:00:13.780
and lives.

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:16.216
And there's just so much environmental

00:00:16.216 --> 00:00:18.518
and humanitarian disaster there.

00:00:19.019 --> 00:00:20.453
What do you know

00:00:20.453 --> 00:00:23.189
about the state of that dam right now?

00:00:24.691 --> 00:00:25.392
Well, obviously,

00:00:25.392 --> 00:00:26.626
there was a significant breach

00:00:26.626 --> 00:00:27.894
that caused all that flooding.

00:00:27.894 --> 00:00:31.164
We still don't have specific information

00:00:31.631 --> 00:00:33.299
about how that breach occurred.

00:00:33.299 --> 00:00:34.100
And we're doing the best

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:35.735
we can talking to Ukrainian authorities

00:00:35.735 --> 00:00:37.270
to try to assess that.

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:38.471
But really, honestly,

00:00:38.471 --> 00:00:40.006
much of our focus right now

00:00:40.006 --> 00:00:40.306
and I mean,

00:00:40.306 --> 00:00:42.008
the predominant amount of our focus

00:00:42.008 --> 00:00:43.376
is on helping

00:00:43.376 --> 00:00:43.943
alleviate

00:00:43.943 --> 00:00:45.412
some of the humanitarian concerns

00:00:45.412 --> 00:00:46.246
that you just mentioned.

00:00:46.246 --> 00:00:48.148
Tens of thousands of Ukrainians

00:00:48.148 --> 00:00:48.882
in southern

00:00:48.882 --> 00:00:50.250
the southern part of the country

00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:51.684
all the way down to crishon,

00:00:51.684 --> 00:00:53.319
are having to evacuate their homes

00:00:53.319 --> 00:00:55.155
and leave their businesses behind.

00:00:55.155 --> 00:00:56.256
There have been casualties.

00:00:56.256 --> 00:00:57.757
Lives have been lost.

00:00:57.757 --> 00:01:00.093
Obviously, there's a lack of water.

00:01:00.093 --> 00:01:01.694
There's a lack of power.

00:01:01.694 --> 00:01:03.363
So we're doing everything we can,

00:01:03.363 --> 00:01:03.930
working through

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:06.066
USAID and our humanitarian partners

00:01:06.066 --> 00:01:06.833
on the ground

00:01:06.833 --> 00:01:08.568
to get aid and assistance

00:01:08.568 --> 00:01:10.136
to where it's needed, in fact.

00:01:10.136 --> 00:01:12.605
Christiane, within hours of the breach,

00:01:12.605 --> 00:01:13.740
USAID had work

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:14.841
with their partners on the ground

00:01:14.841 --> 00:01:15.975
to get busses available

00:01:15.975 --> 00:01:16.943
to just get people

00:01:16.943 --> 00:01:18.411
out of the flood waters

00:01:18.411 --> 00:01:20.080
and get them out of danger.

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:22.348
We have provided boats, water

00:01:22.649 --> 00:01:23.817
purification equipment,

00:01:23.817 --> 00:01:25.351
obviously water itself

00:01:25.351 --> 00:01:26.853
and other rescue gear.

00:01:26.853 --> 00:01:27.921
And so we're going to stay in touch

00:01:27.921 --> 00:01:28.621
with the Ukrainians

00:01:28.621 --> 00:01:29.989
about what they need going forward.

00:01:29.989 --> 00:01:31.591
They can count on the United States

00:01:31.591 --> 00:01:32.492
to continue to support.

00:01:32.492 --> 00:01:33.893
You mentioned water,

00:01:33.893 --> 00:01:35.795
and we understand that

00:01:35.795 --> 00:01:38.431
only you know, sort of shipped

00:01:38.431 --> 00:01:40.200
in water, so to speak,

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:41.734
can be used for drinking.

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:43.970
They're entirely reliant on outside water

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:44.637
coming in.

00:01:44.637 --> 00:01:47.240
President Zelensky has also said publicly

00:01:47.941 --> 00:01:51.611
that Russia is, in fact, firing on people

00:01:51.611 --> 00:01:52.846
who are trying to evacuate

00:01:52.846 --> 00:01:54.881
and on any assistance measures.

00:01:54.881 --> 00:01:55.682
This is what he said

00:01:56.816 --> 00:01:57.550
at least.

00:01:57.784 --> 00:02:00.153
The situation is extremely difficult.

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:02.122
Russian troops do not stop

00:02:02.122 --> 00:02:04.524
artillery strikes at the very territory

00:02:04.524 --> 00:02:06.693
where people are being evacuated aided.

00:02:06.693 --> 00:02:07.861
Unfortunately,

00:02:07.861 --> 00:02:08.628
there are wounded

00:02:08.628 --> 00:02:10.597
from their terrorist attacks.

00:02:10.597 --> 00:02:12.765
People who are rescuing and evacuating

00:02:12.765 --> 00:02:13.466
from the Russian

00:02:13.466 --> 00:02:15.735
ecocide are also forced to flee

00:02:15.735 --> 00:02:18.071
from Russian fire.

00:02:18.738 --> 00:02:19.739
John Kirby,

00:02:19.739 --> 00:02:22.275
there is a lot of anger inside Ukraine

00:02:22.475 --> 00:02:23.810
about the notion

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:26.412
that they may be considered

00:02:26.412 --> 00:02:28.281
you know, responsible for it

00:02:28.281 --> 00:02:28.982
on the one hand.

00:02:28.982 --> 00:02:30.016
On the other hand,

00:02:30.016 --> 00:02:31.151
everybody knows that

00:02:31.151 --> 00:02:32.218
Russia has been

00:02:32.218 --> 00:02:35.054
bombarding this area for a long time

00:02:35.054 --> 00:02:35.855
and the threat to

00:02:35.855 --> 00:02:36.723
this dam

00:02:36.723 --> 00:02:38.658
has been public concern

00:02:38.658 --> 00:02:40.260
for a long, long time.

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:42.195
Do you really think

00:02:42.195 --> 00:02:44.397
that it's anything other than Russia

00:02:45.965 --> 00:02:47.367
Well, we don't really know.

00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:49.068
We just don't know what caused

00:02:49.068 --> 00:02:50.003
the breach of the dam.

00:02:50.003 --> 00:02:50.470
And again,

00:02:50.470 --> 00:02:51.337
we're trying to assess

00:02:51.337 --> 00:02:52.372
that as best we can.

00:02:52.372 --> 00:02:53.540
We're not on the ground

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:54.707
that we're trying to do the best

00:02:54.707 --> 00:02:55.642
we can to assess it.

00:02:55.642 --> 00:02:57.644
I think it's fair to say

00:02:57.644 --> 00:02:59.846
that we all need to recognize

00:02:59.846 --> 00:03:01.381
Russia was illegally

00:03:01.381 --> 00:03:02.549
in that part of Ukraine.

00:03:02.549 --> 00:03:03.716
They have no business being on

00:03:03.716 --> 00:03:05.685
Ukrainian territory, period.

00:03:05.685 --> 00:03:06.886
But we know that they were

00:03:06.886 --> 00:03:08.321
occupying areas

00:03:08.321 --> 00:03:09.722
in that part of southern Ukraine.

00:03:09.722 --> 00:03:11.524
We know that they were occupying

00:03:11.524 --> 00:03:13.426
the dam and the reservoir.

00:03:13.426 --> 00:03:15.161
And so clearly, they have

00:03:15.161 --> 00:03:16.062
clearly they had

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:18.198
given themselves

00:03:18.198 --> 00:03:19.866
illegally, but given themselves

00:03:19.866 --> 00:03:21.434
the mantle of responsibility

00:03:21.434 --> 00:03:22.168
for that dam

00:03:22.168 --> 00:03:23.636
and for the safety of that dam.

00:03:23.636 --> 00:03:25.805
So clearly, in that context, yes, Russia

00:03:26.706 --> 00:03:27.674
certainly bears

00:03:27.674 --> 00:03:29.776
responsibility here in general

00:03:29.776 --> 00:03:31.844
for being just being there physically.

00:03:31.844 --> 00:03:33.780
But what caused the breach exactly.

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:34.981
That's what we just don't know.

00:03:34.981 --> 00:03:35.848
And again,

00:03:35.848 --> 00:03:37.617
while we still want to figure that out,

00:03:37.617 --> 00:03:39.152
we are mainly focused on

00:03:39.152 --> 00:03:40.019
trying to alleviate

00:03:40.019 --> 00:03:41.521
the humanitarian disaster

00:03:41.521 --> 00:03:42.689
that that bridge those costs,

00:03:42.689 --> 00:03:44.490
but is clearly

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:46.292
you know, many believe that

00:03:46.292 --> 00:03:47.794
and certainly the Ukrainians that it

00:03:47.794 --> 00:03:49.062
and I've heard American officials

00:03:49.062 --> 00:03:52.765
say that it could be a very cynical plot

00:03:52.899 --> 00:03:54.601
to or method

00:03:54.601 --> 00:03:56.869
of trying to thwart the counteroffensive

00:03:57.036 --> 00:03:59.906
that we understand is finally underway.

00:04:00.273 --> 00:04:02.842
It would thwart the counteroffensive,

00:04:02.842 --> 00:04:03.243
wouldn't it?

00:04:03.243 --> 00:04:04.244
I mean, how does it

00:04:04.244 --> 00:04:05.612
how does a nation fight

00:04:05.612 --> 00:04:07.947
with all the mod cons that you've sent?

00:04:07.981 --> 00:04:08.514
We understand

00:04:08.514 --> 00:04:10.917
the Bradleys are the armored vehicles

00:04:10.917 --> 00:04:13.119
that you've all sent, are in are in use.

00:04:13.119 --> 00:04:13.319
Right.

00:04:13.319 --> 00:04:14.821
Now, it's very difficult

00:04:14.821 --> 00:04:16.256
for them to come across

00:04:16.256 --> 00:04:18.057
that kind of flooded terrain.

00:04:19.192 --> 00:04:19.459
Well,

00:04:19.459 --> 00:04:19.726
with the

00:04:19.726 --> 00:04:20.393
caveat that

00:04:20.393 --> 00:04:22.161
I won't speak for the Ukrainian military

00:04:22.161 --> 00:04:22.495
or what

00:04:22.495 --> 00:04:23.796
their plans or intentions

00:04:23.796 --> 00:04:26.199
are in terms of offensive operations,

00:04:26.199 --> 00:04:27.900
that's really for them to speak to.

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:28.635
Certainly,

00:04:28.635 --> 00:04:30.670
if you just look at the flooding

00:04:30.670 --> 00:04:32.538
that it was caused south

00:04:32.538 --> 00:04:34.807
into the southwest of the dam

00:04:35.041 --> 00:04:35.475
through that

00:04:35.475 --> 00:04:36.809
southern part of Ukraine, downed

00:04:36.809 --> 00:04:37.877
a course on,

00:04:37.877 --> 00:04:40.079
clearly that kind of flooding

00:04:40.213 --> 00:04:42.782
is going to have an impact on militaries

00:04:43.483 --> 00:04:45.885
ability to maneuver and to fight.

00:04:45.918 --> 00:04:47.220
I mean, just the flooding itself

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:49.188
will will make conditions

00:04:49.188 --> 00:04:51.457
on an untenable

00:04:51.457 --> 00:04:52.458
for that kind of fighting.

00:04:52.458 --> 00:04:53.192
But also, it's

00:04:53.192 --> 00:04:53.860
going to

00:04:53.893 --> 00:04:56.362
necessarily as it has diverted

00:04:56.362 --> 00:04:58.931
Ukrainian resources and energy

00:04:59.198 --> 00:05:00.566
and even some of their,

00:05:00.566 --> 00:05:00.867
you know,

00:05:00.867 --> 00:05:01.934
their military's attention

00:05:01.934 --> 00:05:03.069
to trying to help alleviate

00:05:03.069 --> 00:05:04.470
the humanitarian catastrophe.

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:05.972
So in that regard, certainly

00:05:05.972 --> 00:05:08.207
there's going to be an impact to Ukraine.

00:05:08.207 --> 00:05:09.542
And so they're resourcing in there

00:05:09.542 --> 00:05:11.077
and they're in their ability.

00:05:11.077 --> 00:05:11.611
But again,

00:05:11.611 --> 00:05:12.545
there is a lot of fighting

00:05:12.545 --> 00:05:14.147
going on elsewhere

00:05:14.147 --> 00:05:15.915
in the eastern part of the country.

00:05:15.915 --> 00:05:17.016
And we'll let Mr.

00:05:17.016 --> 00:05:19.052
Zelenskiy speak to to that

00:05:19.052 --> 00:05:19.886
and to characterize.

00:05:19.886 --> 00:05:20.853
So even,

00:05:20.853 --> 00:05:22.655
you know, I know you will let him but

00:05:22.655 --> 00:05:23.756
but we've heard

00:05:23.756 --> 00:05:24.490
and we've read

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:26.059
and we know that you have

00:05:26.059 --> 00:05:28.494
obviously many intelligence

00:05:28.494 --> 00:05:29.762
and eyes on the ground.

00:05:29.762 --> 00:05:31.197
The Russian president has said

00:05:31.197 --> 00:05:33.833
that the counteroffensive has started

00:05:33.833 --> 00:05:35.868
and that it's not going well for Ukraine.

00:05:35.868 --> 00:05:37.503
And we've heard separately from U.S.

00:05:37.503 --> 00:05:39.572
officials that there's been a lot of

00:05:40.139 --> 00:05:41.641
fight back by the Russians

00:05:41.641 --> 00:05:43.276
and quite a lot of casualties

00:05:43.276 --> 00:05:45.511
in terms of material and men.

00:05:45.745 --> 00:05:46.679
What can you tell us

00:05:46.679 --> 00:05:48.581
about the initial stages

00:05:48.581 --> 00:05:50.783
of of this counteroffensive?

00:05:51.951 --> 00:05:52.118
Well,

00:05:52.118 --> 00:05:52.752
again, I'll let the

00:05:52.752 --> 00:05:54.053
Ukrainians speak to their

00:05:54.053 --> 00:05:55.254
their offensive operations.

00:05:55.254 --> 00:05:56.122
We wouldn't do that.

00:05:56.122 --> 00:05:57.156
We wouldn't characterize it.

00:05:57.156 --> 00:05:57.957
And we wouldn't

00:05:57.957 --> 00:05:58.291
we wouldn't

00:05:58.291 --> 00:05:59.625
get ahead of President Zelensky.

00:05:59.625 --> 00:06:00.993
But clearly

00:06:01.327 --> 00:06:03.363
and you have CNN reporters on the ground

00:06:03.363 --> 00:06:05.598
witnessing this for themselves, there is

00:06:06.032 --> 00:06:07.467
there is stepped up

00:06:07.467 --> 00:06:10.737
fighting along that eastern flank there

00:06:11.304 --> 00:06:13.406
along the eastern side of the country

00:06:13.639 --> 00:06:15.074
all the way from Donbas

00:06:15.074 --> 00:06:16.709
and including around back in

00:06:16.709 --> 00:06:18.644
and points further south.

00:06:18.644 --> 00:06:20.113
And so there is there is contact

00:06:20.113 --> 00:06:21.681
between these two military forces

00:06:21.681 --> 00:06:22.348
there is fighting.

00:06:22.348 --> 00:06:23.950
There have been casualties.

00:06:23.950 --> 00:06:25.151
And what we're going to be focused

00:06:25.151 --> 00:06:25.718
on, again,

00:06:25.718 --> 00:06:27.487
without characterizing what they're doing

00:06:27.487 --> 00:06:28.554
or speaking for them,

00:06:28.554 --> 00:06:29.422
but we're we're going to stay

00:06:29.422 --> 00:06:31.090
focused on is making sure

00:06:31.090 --> 00:06:32.925
that they have all the resources,

00:06:32.925 --> 00:06:34.427
the capabilities, the training,

00:06:34.427 --> 00:06:35.261
the tools that they need

00:06:35.261 --> 00:06:36.062
to be successful

00:06:36.062 --> 00:06:37.063
in the weeks and months ahead.

00:06:37.063 --> 00:06:38.731
And that includes, Christiane,

00:06:38.731 --> 00:06:39.499
in coming days,

00:06:39.499 --> 00:06:39.766
I think

00:06:39.766 --> 00:06:40.533
you'll see

00:06:40.533 --> 00:06:41.334
some more announcements

00:06:41.334 --> 00:06:43.503
from the United States about additional

00:06:43.503 --> 00:06:44.537
aid and security

00:06:44.537 --> 00:06:44.971
and weapons

00:06:44.971 --> 00:06:45.671
and capabilities

00:06:45.671 --> 00:06:46.739
that will be going to

00:06:46.739 --> 00:06:49.075
the Ukrainian armed forces to help them.

00:06:49.075 --> 00:06:50.176
Another ominous

00:06:51.177 --> 00:06:52.111
pledge

00:06:52.111 --> 00:06:53.613
from President Putin

00:06:53.613 --> 00:06:55.648
was that in a matter of days,

00:06:55.648 --> 00:06:57.517
he is going to deploy

00:06:57.517 --> 00:06:59.719
tactical nuclear weapons to Belarus.

00:06:59.886 --> 00:07:02.155
He says that they've built the

00:07:02.155 --> 00:07:03.756
whatever they need to build

00:07:03.756 --> 00:07:05.191
to house these things.

00:07:05.191 --> 00:07:07.093
What can the United States do about that?

00:07:07.093 --> 00:07:08.995
Have you demolished Belarus?

00:07:08.995 --> 00:07:09.962
Well, what is the

00:07:09.962 --> 00:07:12.465
what is the actual real threat of them

00:07:12.465 --> 00:07:14.634
being in Belarus?

00:07:14.867 --> 00:07:18.504
This is another example of just reckless

00:07:18.504 --> 00:07:19.639
and irresponsible

00:07:19.639 --> 00:07:20.373
rhetoric and

00:07:20.373 --> 00:07:21.808
and and posturing

00:07:21.808 --> 00:07:23.810
about nuclear capabilities from Mr.

00:07:23.810 --> 00:07:27.213
Putin and from Moscow.

00:07:27.213 --> 00:07:29.549
A nuclear war can should never be fought,

00:07:29.549 --> 00:07:30.850
can never be won.

00:07:30.850 --> 00:07:33.052
We've been very clear about that.

00:07:33.052 --> 00:07:34.353
This is dangerous rhetoric,

00:07:34.353 --> 00:07:36.222
which we have to take seriously.

00:07:36.222 --> 00:07:39.659
We can't just cast it off as bluster.

00:07:39.692 --> 00:07:40.426
We have to take it

00:07:40.426 --> 00:07:42.361
seriously coming from a country

00:07:42.361 --> 00:07:43.863
like Russia and from Mr. Putin.

00:07:43.863 --> 00:07:44.730
So we're doing the best

00:07:44.730 --> 00:07:46.098
we can to monitor.

00:07:46.098 --> 00:07:47.600
We don't see anything out there

00:07:47.600 --> 00:07:49.101
that shows us that there's

00:07:49.101 --> 00:07:50.870
an imminent indication of movement

00:07:50.870 --> 00:07:52.004
of nuclear capabilities

00:07:52.004 --> 00:07:54.507
or imminent risk of of nuclear

00:07:55.107 --> 00:07:56.375
war inside Ukraine

00:07:56.375 --> 00:07:58.444
or even on the continent.

00:07:58.444 --> 00:08:00.379
And I can tell you that we've

00:08:00.379 --> 00:08:01.380
we've seen nothing

00:08:01.380 --> 00:08:02.315
that would cause us

00:08:02.315 --> 00:08:04.684
to change our own deterrent posture

00:08:04.684 --> 00:08:05.785
when it comes to those kinds

00:08:05.785 --> 00:08:06.486
of capabilities.

00:08:06.486 --> 00:08:07.687
And we're watching this

00:08:07.687 --> 00:08:08.521
very, very closely.

